WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:06.580 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it came to pass in the year of Christ  1260 when Baldwin was raining at  Constantinople at Messer Nicholas polo  the father of my lord mark and Messer  Maffeo polo the brother of messin  Achilles were at that said city of  Constantinople whither they had gone  from Venice with their merchants where's  now these two brethren men singularly  noble wise and Provident took counsel  together to cross the greater sea on a  venture of trade so they laid in a store  of jewels and set forth from  Constantinople crossing the sea to  saltier  [Music]  having stayed a while at Seoul dear they  considered the matter and thought it  well to extend their journey further so  they set forth from Seoul dia and  traveled till they came to the court of  a certain tartar Prince Barca con by  name whose residences were at Zara and  at bol Gaara and who was esteemed one of  the most liberal and courteous Prince's  that ever was amongst the Tartars this  Barker was delighted at the arrival of  the two brothers and treated them there  with great honour  so they presented to him the whole of  the jewels that they had brought with  them the prince was highly pleased with  these and accepted the offering most  graciously causing the brothers to  receive at least twice its value after  they had spent a twelvemonth at the  court of this Prince they broke out a  great war between Barker and allow the  Lord of the Tartars of the Levant and  great hosts were mustered on either side  but in the end Barker the Lord of the  Tartars of the ponent was defeated  though on both sides there was great  slaughter and by reason of this war  no one could travel without peril of  being taken thus it was at least on the  road by which the brothers had come  though there was no obstacle to their  traveling forward so the brothers  finding they could not retrace their  steps determined to go forward  [Music]  quitting Bulgaria therefore they  proceeded to a city named Oaxaca which  was at the extremity of the kingdom of  the Lord of the potent and thence  departing again and passing the great  river tigris they traveled across a  desert which extended for 17 days  journey and wherein they found neither  town nor village falling in only with  the tents of Tartars occupied with their  cattle at pasture  after they had passed the desert they  arrived at a very great and noble city  noon to Pokhara the territory of which  belongs to a king whose name was Barack  and is also called Baqarah  the city is the best in all of Persia  and when they had got thither they found  they could neither proceed further  forward nor yet turned back again  wherefore they abode in that city of  acara  for three years and whilst they were so  joining in that city there came from  allow Lord of the Levant envoys on their  way to the court of the Great Khan the  Lord of all the Tatars in the world and  when the end voice held the two brothers  they were amazed for they had never  before seen Athens in that part of the  world and they said to the brothers  gentlemen if you will take our counsel  ye will find great honour and profit  shall come thereof so they replied that  they would be right glad to learn how in  truth said the end voice the Great Khan  have never seen any Latins and he hath a  great desire to do so wherefore if ye  will keep us company to his court he may  depend upon it that he will be right  glad to see you and will treat you with  great honor and liberality whilst in our  company ye shall travel with perfect  security and need fear to be molested by  nobody  [Music]  you

